                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e5a1ca87-2d40-3a17-bf98-f520ef891096",
                        "entry_id": "cce2602d-5f60-328c-81de-161dd6b63dee",
                        "glosses": [
                            "(real analysis): Given a subset X of R, the smallest real number that is ≥ every element of X; (order theory): given a subset X of a partially ordered set P (with partial order ≤), the least element y of P such that every element of X is ≤ y."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "195a5bcd-c116-446d-ba24-27dc6435b144",
                                "sense_id": "e5a1ca87-2d40-3a17-bf98-f520ef891096",
                                "text": "A sublattice of a lattice is a subset that is closed under pairwise infima and suprema."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a597788-808b-4d8f-a8d4-9c767b09e057",
                                "sense_id": "e5a1ca87-2d40-3a17-bf98-f520ef891096",
                                "text": "The best way to describe the supremum of S is to say that it wants to be the greatest element of S. In fact, if S has a greatest element, then that element is the supremum."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6eb1e044-bf3b-4498-b538-329195427b92",
                                "sense_id": "e5a1ca87-2d40-3a17-bf98-f520ef891096",
                                "text": "The key to an approach to vector optimization based on infimum and supremum is to consider set-based objective functions and to extend the partial ordering of the original objective space to a suitable subspace of the power set. In this new space the infimum and supremum exist under the usual assumptions."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0eb59cf5-d0e7-4e81-ad7f-3f390bc12717",
                        "source_entry_id": "cce2602d-5f60-328c-81de-161dd6b63dee",
                        "source_sense_id": "e5a1ca87-2d40-3a17-bf98-f520ef891096",
